cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AeroTraj-Ultra: Physics-Grounded Non-Autoregressive Flight Trajectory Prediction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the original papers it builds on (FlightBERT, IEEE TITS 2023; FlightBERT++, AAAI 2024; MAF-Net, AAMAS 2026) as well as this work."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Valle"
    given-names: "Marco"
    email: "marco.valle2002@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<USERNAME>/AeroTraj-Ultra"
url: "https://github.com/<USERNAME>/AeroTraj-Ultra"
abstract: >-
  AeroTraj-Ultra is a 1.28M-parameter non-autoregressive multi-horizon regressor for
  short-term 4D aircraft trajectory prediction (5-300 s) from ADS-B. It combines a
  Gray-Code lattice decoder with a differentiable straight-through prefix-parity
  soft-XOR, a continuous residual head anchored on a closed-form damped
  coordinated-turn kinematic prior, and a MAF-Net differentiable trust-region gate
  that bounds the influence of the Gray-Code branch. Trained on up to 180
  consecutive days of real OpenSky traffic on a single RTX 4070, it reaches
  991.6 m of 3-D ECEF mean distance error over the 5-300 s horizon, the best
  among ten compared models (FlightBERT++ V2, Deep LSTM, constant velocity,
  Conditional Flow Matching, ASCENT, Attention-LSTM, IMM+neural residual, DDPM/MID).
keywords:
  - aircraft trajectory prediction
  - ADS-B
  - OpenSky
  - transformer
  - gray code
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - flight trajectory prediction
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
